<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saluva Narasimha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1491">1491</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Saluva Narasimha Deva Raya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saluva Narasimha Deva Raya was a Vijayanagara general and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragiri">Chandragiri</a> who seized the throne from the last weak Sangama ruler around 1485, founding the short-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saluva-dynasty">Saluva dynasty</a>. He fought the Gajapatis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> to restore the empire's frontiers and imported horses for its cavalry through the western ports. He died in 1491, leaving his young sons in the care of his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narasa-nayaka">Narasa Nayaka</a>.</p></div>
